# THE CHOICE REPORT (F1 of the 2026-10-13 fail-closed pass, verbatim: «`native-json-run` on a program with a consulted
# choice site answers `ok` with the canonical member and nothing marks it»; lane cli/consumption-marker-1013, [AGENT]).
# DEFAULT (zero replay): the run is made on the tape padded with 2^20 zeros and the consultation count is read off the
# leftover; one stderr line when it is non-zero, nothing when zero, and on a Stop ending (no leftover) a line saying the
# count is unavailable. `--choice-report=full` adds `choice-trace`'s pass (sites and bounds; refuses on disagreement).
# `--no-choice-report` silences it. Fixture Tests/wire-boundary-choicereport/main.go. The streams are captured
# SEPARATELY: stdout must be byte-identical to the --no-choice-report run (the observation never changes), and the flag
# leaves stderr empty. The canonical member is in the enumerator's set; the flags are native-json-run's alone.
